{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1223878-rules-clarification-merit-cost","id":1223878,"title":"Rules Clarification: Merit Cost","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-01T04:37:16-07:00","id":1223878,"title":"Rules Clarification: Merit Cost","content":"Really basic question here about something that the rulebook doesn't make quite clear enough.<br /> <br /> When buying Merits that have multiple dots, is the cost calculated according to the total number of dots or is the price cumulative?<br /> <br /> For example, if a character wants to buy the Familiar Merit but wants to get a Rank 2 Spirit (which counts as a four dot Familiar), does he have to pay the two-dot price first *then* pay the four-dot price on top of that, or does he pay the XP cost for all four dots at once?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/413-seito-akai","name":"Seito Akai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar413_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T04:53:40-07:00","id":1223880,"title":"","content":"In your example you'd only pay 4 XP. Even if he upgrades from two dots to four dots he only needs to pay for the additional dots.<br /> It's the same for Style Merits as well. If you already have the first dot in a Fighting Style and wants to buy the second dot, you only pay one XP for that dot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T05:02:55-07:00","id":1223883,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s pretty clear in the book each dot of a Merit costs 1 XP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T07:45:33-07:00","id":1223908,"title":"","content":"Seito Akai is asking about Merits that have multiple levels. So if he wants to buy Strikings Looks 2, would that cost 2 XP, or 1+2=3 XP?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T07:57:36-07:00","id":1223911,"title":"","content":"Merits with extra levels are simply building on the benefits of previous levels, you can\u2019t have a higher level Merit without having already purchased the lower level version.<br /> <br /> This is simple addition.<br /> <br /> If you purchase a dot in a Merit it costs 1 XP, you don\u2019t repurchase anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T12:33:15-07:00","id":1223979,"title":"","content":"Important clarification: this works differently between first and second edition. <b>In first edition,</b> you would separately purchase each dot level of a Merit, even dots that did nothing (like Striking Looks 1). Each dot would cost twice its rating in XP, so for example, if you wanted to buy Striking Looks 2, you would pay 2xp + 4xp = 6xp.<br /> <br /> <b>In second edition,</b> you still purchase even dots that do nothing, but each dot only costs a flat one experience, regardless of how high the dot rating is. Buying Striking Looks 2 in second edition simply costs you 1 + 1 = 2 experiences. Buying up to Familiar 4 from nothing costs 1 + 1 + 1 + 1 = 4 experiences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T13:24:52-07:00","id":1223988,"title":"","content":"That's only a change in how XP works (disregarding the old MET CofD books). In both 1e and 2e, if you're buying a 3 dot Merit, it doesn't matter if it has functions at 1, 2 and 3 dots, only has function at 3 dots, or only has functions at 1 dot and 3 dots. You buy each dot, and having 3 dots in the Merit always costs the same amount of XP. 1e had increasing costs, but 3 dots in a Merit was always 12 XP total, regardless of the number of things the Merit does, and in 2e 3 dots in a Merit is always 3 XPs total regardless ofthe number of things the Merit does.<br /> <br /> In 2e, if the authors want to make things a bit more expensive, they're turn it into two Merits. We see this frequently with combat Merits that aren't part of styles (ex: Cheap Shot, Iron Skin), or supernatural upgrades (Advanced and Epic versions of Merits).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}